@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# Replace SendGrid SDKs with direct HTTP
+
+Verified the premise before editing: repository searches found SendGrid imports only in `email.go` and first-party Bazel dependency labels only in this directory's BUILD. Checked the pinned SDK implementations (`sendgrid-go` v3.16.1 and `rest` v2.6.9) for JSON encoding, default host, headers, context propagation, and response-body handling.
+
+The client now marshals a small private SendGrid request type and posts using the existing injected `http.Client` (defaulting to `httpclient.New`). Preserved validation, sender fallback, one personalization per recipient, omitted empty display names, HTML content, default/override host, headers, context cancellation, successful 2xx statuses, and Unavailable errors including non-2xx response bodies. Response bodies are read and closed on success and failure. The SDK's unreachable nil-response guard is unnecessary because `http.Client.Do` guarantees a non-nil response/body when its error is nil.
+
+Updated BUILD by removing three SDK labels. Existing httptest cases verify authorization, content type, JSON fields, sender fallback/override, recipient privacy, validation and HTTP 500 errors. Added HTTP 200, 300 and 401 cases, canceled-context coverage, and rejection of unknown JSON fields in the fake.
+
+## Measurements
+
+Same script run against original files copied from HEAD into `/tmp/email-before` and the edited directory:
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+for directory in ['/tmp/email-before', 'enterprise/server/backends/email']:
+    p = Path(directory)
+    b = (p / 'BUILD').read_text()
+    g = (p / 'email.go').read_text()
+    print(directory,
+          'targets', len(re.findall(r'^    name =', b, re.M)),
+          'deps', len(re.findall(r'^        "', b, re.M)),
+          'external labels', len(re.findall(r'^        "@', b, re.M)),
+          'SDK modules', len(set(re.findall(r'github.com/sendgrid/([^/"\s]+)', g))),
+          'LOC', [len((p / f).read_text().splitlines())
+                  for f in ['email.go', 'email_test.go', 'BUILD']])
+```
+
+| Metric (email package only) | Before | After |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Bazel targets | 2 | 2 |
+| Direct BUILD dependency labels | 9 | 6 |
+| External BUILD dependency labels | 4 | 1 |
+| Direct SendGrid modules used | 2 | 0 |
+| Source LOC | 160 | 188 |
+| Test LOC | 270 | 312 |
+| BUILD LOC | 28 | 25 |
+
+This removes two module usages, not declarations from go.mod. Local source grows by 28 lines to replace the SDK payload and transport helpers; binary size and transitive dependency savings were not measured.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `gofmt -w enterprise/server/backends/email/{email.go,email_test.go}` and `git diff --check`: clean.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(//..., //enterprise/server/backends/email:all, 1)'`: failed (exit 7) after loading 3,421 packages because unrelated `+dockerfile_image+default_execution_image` hit its Docker build timeout. Did not stop the scoped code checks because of this repository setup failure.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(set(//enterprise/server/backends/email:all //enterprise/server/backends/email/sendmail:all //enterprise/server/notification:all //enterprise/server/usagealert:all), //enterprise/server/backends/email:all, 1)'`: passed (exit 0). The universe was selected using `rg '"//enterprise/server/backends/email"' --glob BUILD`, which identifies every first-party direct user. Returned:
+  - `//enterprise/server/backends/email:email`
+  - `//enterprise/server/backends/email:email_test`
+  - `//enterprise/server/backends/email/sendmail:sendmail_lib`
+  - `//enterprise/server/notification:notification`
+  - `//enterprise/server/notification:notification_test`
+  - `//enterprise/server/usagealert:usagealert_lib`
+  - `//enterprise/server/usagealert:usagealert_test`
+- `bazel test //enterprise/server/backends/email:email_test --jobs=2`: initially failed build-time static analysis S1016 (use direct struct conversion); applied the suggested conversion and reran the same command: passed (exit 0), one test target passed.
+- `bazel test //enterprise/server/backends/email:email //enterprise/server/backends/email:email_test //enterprise/server/backends/email/sendmail:sendmail_lib //enterprise/server/notification:notification //enterprise/server/notification:notification_test //enterprise/server/usagealert:usagealert_lib //enterprise/server/usagealert:usagealert_test --jobs=2`: initially failed (exit 36), unable to create a sandbox because the 25 GB disk was full. `docker builder prune -f` removed unused build cache and restored about 3.4 GB of free disk space. Reran the identical command: passed (exit 0), all four library targets built and all three test targets passed (email cached; notification and usagealert executed). Final retry log: `/tmp/email-rdeps-test-retry.log`.
+
+Long Bazel tests and the scoped query ran under `nohup sh -c '... > /tmp/email-*.log 2>&1; echo $? > /tmp/email-*.exit'` with the launcher waiting in a tool session, and logs were polled. The full query ran in a persistent tool session.
+
+## External dependencies and scope
+
+After editing, `rg 'github.com/sendgrid/|@com_github_sendgrid_' --glob '*.go' --glob BUILD .` returns no matches (exit 1). Both `github.com/sendgrid/sendgrid-go` and `github.com/sendgrid/rest` therefore have no remaining first-party Go or BUILD users. The module declarations and repository registrations remain for the separate serialized dependency-removal PR. No shared dependency files were edited. All changes, including this report, are within `enterprise/server/backends/email/`. No push or PR.
